Audio samples ship in three sets, under three different terms.


samples/salamander/ and samples/salamander-lowlatency/
------------------------------------------------------

Derived from the Salamander Drumkit by Alexander Holm, released under the
Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Unported license (CC BY 3.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/

The files in this repository have been trimmed, level-matched, and
reorganized for low-latency playback. They remain licensed under CC BY 3.0.

Attribution: Salamander Drumkit by Alexander Holm, CC BY 3.0.


samples/tr808/
--------------

Derived from the Roland TR-808 Sound Sample Set 1.0.0 (1994) by Michael
Fischer, as published by the TidalCycles project under the Creative Commons
CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication:
https://github.com/tidalcycles/sounds-tr808-fischer
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

The files here were trimmed to their transient, resampled from 44.1 kHz to
48 kHz in the frequency domain, normalized, and written as 24-bit stereo by
tools/build_kit_b.py. CC0 imposes no conditions, so no attribution is
required; it is recorded here because knowing where a sound came from is
worth more than the licence requires.


samples/impact/
---------------

Generated by tools/build_kit_b.py rather than recorded: inharmonic partials,
a filtered noise transient, and scattered grains for the debris tail. Part of
this project and covered by the repository's LICENSE.
